[h1]Welcome Note[/h1]

Spawns a customizable welcome note in every new character's inventory. Perfect for communicating server rules, tips, community info, or lore to new players.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*] Automatically gives a readable note to every new character
[*] Note content loaded from a simple text file on the server
[*] Multi-page support using [b]<PAGE>[/b] delimiter
[*] Configurable note title via Sandbox Options
[*] Multiplayer compatible (server→client architecture)
[*] No dependencies
[/list]

[h2]Setup[/h2]
[olist]
[*] Subscribe and add [b]\welcomenote[/b] to your server's [b]Mods=[/b] line
[*] Create a text file at [b]<cachedir>/Lua/welcome-note.txt[/b] with your note content
[*] (Optional) Set the note title in Sandbox Options under "Welcome Note"
[*] Restart the server
[/olist]

[h2]File Format[/h2]
Place your note content in [b]Lua/welcome-note.txt[/b] inside your server's cache directory. Use [b]<PAGE>[/b] to separate pages:

[code]
Welcome to our server!

Rules:
- Be polite
- No griefing
<PAGE>
Tips:
- Generators need fuel
- Join our Discord at discord.gg/example
<PAGE>
Have fun surviving!
[/code]

[h2]Limits[/h2]
[list]
[*] Maximum [b]20 pages[/b] per note
[*] Maximum [b]16,384 characters[/b] per page
[*] Content is cached on server start — changes require a server restart
[/list]

[h2]Recommended: Auto-Cleanup[/h2]
Players may drop the welcome note on the ground. To auto-remove dropped notes, add [b]WelcomeNote.WelcomeNote[/b] to your [b]WorldItemRemovalList[/b] in SandboxVars:

[code]
WorldItemRemovalList = "Base.Hat,Base.Glasses,WelcomeNote.WelcomeNote",
[/code]

[h2]Sandbox Options[/h2]
[table]
[tr][th]Option[/th][th]Default[/th][th]Description[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Note Title[/td][td]Welcome to the Server![/td][td]The display name of the note in the player's inventory[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*] Project Zomboid Build 42.20+
[*] Multiplayer dedicated servers and singleplayer
[*] No dependencies
[*] Does not conflict with other mods
[/list]

